IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc15-general`

-- ccc15-tests-general.l4 -- tests for ccc15-general.l4 (sections 468 to 475). Every expected value is written here from the text before the run,
-- beside its assertion, and not copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests for section 468`

-- 468: a superior court of criminal jurisdiction (as s 2 says) has jurisdiction to try any indictable offence.
#ASSERT `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an indictable offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a summary conviction offence is outside "any indictable offence": not covered
#ASSERT `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an offence punishable on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING
-- an offence that is both indictable and summary: the text is silent
#ASSERT `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a superior court: the grant is to "every superior court", the text says nothing of other courts
#ASSERT `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST FALSE) `an indictable offence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2 not determined: points outside
#ASSERT `s 468 the superior court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` NOTHING `an indictable offence` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 469`

-- The charge builder. `Provision of the Code OF section, subsection`.
GIVEN sec IS A NUMBER
      form IS A `s 469 form of the charge`
      cahwca IS A BOOLEAN
      judge IS A BOOLEAN
      accessory IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 469 facts of the charge`
`s 469 test: a charge` MEANS
    `s 469 facts of the charge` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF sec, ""), form, cahwca, judge, accessory

-- (a): the offence itself under section 47, 51, 53, 61, 74, 75 or 235 (the text's (a)(i), (iii) to (viii); (ii) is repealed)
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 47 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 51 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 53 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 61 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 74 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 75 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 235 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- sections next to the listed ones are not listed
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 48 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 52 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 236 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 234 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- attempted murder is section 239, not listed
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 239 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the subsection is not read: 235(1)
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 facts of the charge` OF (`Provision of the Code` OF 235, "(1)"), `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 469(a)(i) names section 47 only: a charge named by section 46 (the text creates high treason there, line 854) is in none of (a) to (e), as the section numbers stand (NOTES.md, finding 2)
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 46 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c): section 119 by the holder of a judicial office; by anyone else it is not listed
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 119 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 119 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- being the holder of a judicial office is not enough for another section
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 120 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c.1): an offence under sections 4 to 7 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act; the section named is not read
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 1 `s 469 the charge is of the offence itself` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b): accessory after the fact to high treason, treason or murder
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 235 `s 469 the charge is of being an accessory after the fact to the offence named` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 220 `s 469 the charge is of being an accessory after the fact to the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d): attempting to commit an offence in (a)(i) to (vii): sections 47, 51, 53, 61, 74, 75
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 47 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 51 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 53 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 61 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 74 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 75 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- attempting to commit murder: (d) stops at (a)(vii), so section 235 is not in it
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 235 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- attempting an offence under section 119 by a judicial office holder: not in (d)
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 119 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 48 `s 469 the charge is of attempting to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e): conspiring to commit any offence in paragraph (a), murder included
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 235 `s 469 the charge is of conspiring to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 47 `s 469 the charge is of conspiring to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 74 `s 469 the charge is of conspiring to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 119 `s 469 the charge is of conspiring to commit the offence named` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 48 `s 469 the charge is of conspiring to commit the offence named` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another form (counselling) is in none of (a) to (e)
#ASSERT `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (`s 469 test: a charge` 235 `s 469 the charge is of another form (for example counselling)` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a)(ii) is repealed: the text shows only the note
#ASSERT `s 469(a)(ii) as the text shows it` EQUALS "(ii) [Repealed, 2018, c. 29, s. 61]"

-- The court of criminal jurisdiction's grant: an indictable offence other than the listed ones.
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an indictable offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a listed offence is carved out by "other than"
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- whether the offence is listed is not determined
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an indictable offence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a court of criminal jurisdiction (s 2 says no): the grant does not speak to it
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST FALSE) `an indictable offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` NOTHING `an indictable offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a summary conviction offence, or one that is both: the grant is to "an indictable offence"
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 469 the court of criminal jurisdiction has jurisdiction to try the offence` (JUST TRUE) `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 470`

-- 470: found / arrested / in custody within the territorial jurisdiction ((a)); ordered to be tried by that court or by another whose jurisdiction was transferred ((b)).
-- Arguments: power (s 468 or 469), another provision limits, found, arrested, in custody, ordered by that court, ordered by a court whose jurisdiction was transferred.
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of (a) or (b): an "if" on a grant, unmet: not covered
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the court has no power to try the offence (s 468/469 say no), or that is not determined
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Subject to this Act": another provision limits (or that is not determined): this section does not decide
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 470 the court is competent to try the accused for the offence` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 471`

-- 471: an indictable offence is tried by judge and jury except where the law expressly provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 471 the accused shall be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the exception is met
#ASSERT `s 471 the accused shall be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not determined whether the law provides otherwise
#ASSERT `s 471 the accused shall be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an indictable offence` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a summary conviction offence, or one that is both: not "an indictable offence"
#ASSERT `s 471 the accused shall be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 471 the accused shall be tried by a court composed of a judge and jury` `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 472`

#ASSERT `s 472 as the text shows it` EQUALS "472 [Repealed, R.S., 1985, c. 27 (1st Supp.), s. 63]"

§ `Tests for section 473`

-- 473(1): a listed offence, both consent, a judge of a superior court: may be tried without a jury.
-- Arguments: listed, the accused consents, the AG consents, the trial is by a judge of a superior court.
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the offence is not listed: the grant is for "an offence listed in section 469"
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- either consent missing: "with the consent of the accused and the Attorney General"
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 473(1) the accused may be tried without a jury by a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- 473(1.1): where the consent is given in accordance with (1), the judge may order that any offence be tried in conjunction.
#ASSERT `s 473(1.1) the judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 473(1.1) the judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 473(1.1) the judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction may order that any offence be tried by that judge in conjunction with the offence listed in section 469` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- 473(2): the consent shall not be withdrawn unless both agree. The function is the bar: JUST TRUE means the withdrawal is barred.
#ASSERT `s 473(2) the withdrawal of the consent is barred` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- both agree: the "unless" is met
#ASSERT `s 473(2) the withdrawal of the consent is barred` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the consent was not given in accordance with (1): the "where" fails
#ASSERT `s 473(2) the withdrawal of the consent is barred` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 473(2) the withdrawal of the consent is barred` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 474`

-- 474(1): the clerk may adjourn on the opening day, where no jury panel is to be summoned, if a judge is not present.
-- Arguments: the person is the clerk (s 2), no panel to be summoned, it is the opening day, a judge is present.
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a judge is present: the "if" on a power fails
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no determination that a panel is not to be summoned: the "where" fails
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not the day of the opening: the period fails
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not the clerk (s 2 says no, or says nothing)
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 474(1) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day` NOTHING TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 474(2): a clerk may, at any time, on the instructions of a judge, adjourn.
#ASSERT `s 474(2) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day on the instructions of a judge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 474(2) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day on the instructions of a judge` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 474(2) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day on the instructions of a judge` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 474(2) the clerk of the court may adjourn the court and the business of the court to a subsequent day on the instructions of a judge` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for section 475`

-- 475(1)(a): the accused who absconds is deemed to have waived the right to be present.
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(a) the accused is deemed to have waived the right to be present at the trial` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(a) the accused is deemed to have waived the right to be present at the trial` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(1)(b)(i): the court may continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict.
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may continue the trial and proceed to a judgment or verdict` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(1)(b)(i): sentence in absence, if it finds the accused guilty.
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may impose a sentence on the accused in the accused's absence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may impose a sentence on the accused in the accused's absence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(i) the court may impose a sentence on the accused in the accused's absence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(1)(b)(ii): adjourn to await appearance, if a warrant in Form 7 is issued.
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court may adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court may adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 475(1)(b)(ii) the court may adjourn the trial to await the accused's appearance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(1) proviso: where adjourned under (b)(ii), the court may at any time continue if satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 475(1) the court may, at any time, continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(1) the court may, at any time, continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 475(1) the court may, at any time, continue a trial adjourned pursuant to subparagraph (b)(ii)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(2): where the court continues the trial under (1), it may draw an adverse inference.
#ASSERT `s 475(2) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(2) the court may draw an inference adverse to the accused from the fact that the accused has absconded` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(3): not entitled to re-opening unless the court is satisfied (exceptional circumstances).
#ASSERT `s 475(3) the accused is not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in the accused's absence re-opened` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(3) the accused is not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in the accused's absence re-opened` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 475(3) the accused is not entitled to have any part of the proceedings conducted in the accused's absence re-opened` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 475(4): counsel is not thereby deprived of authority where the accused absconded and the court continues.
#ASSERT `s 475(4) the subsection preserves any authority counsel for the accused has to continue to act for the accused in the proceedings` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 475(4) the subsection preserves any authority counsel for the accused has to continue to act for the accused in the proceedings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 475(4) the subsection preserves any authority counsel for the accused has to continue to act for the accused in the proceedings` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
